<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">ZB vz. 26</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1926</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The ZB vz. 26 was a light machine gun designed by Václav Holek at the Zbrojovka <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a> arms works and adopted by the Czechoslovak army in 1926. Reliable and easy to maintain, it was exported widely and used by many armies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Its design was the basis of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bren-light-machine-gun">Bren gun</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zb-vz-26.jpg" alt="ZB vz. 26" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vitaly V. Kuzmin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ZB_vz._26_at_Great_Patriotic_War_museum_in_Smolensk.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
